The 4 Core Types of Joins
INNER JOIN + LEFT JOIN + RIGHT JOIN + FULL JOIN

INNER JOIN	Only rows that have a perfect match on both sides.
LEFT JOIN	All rows from the first (left) table. Unmatched right side is NULL.
RIGHT JOIN	All rows from the second (right) table. Unmatched left side is NULL.
FULL JOIN	All rows from both tables, filling NULL wherever a match is missing.


INNER JOIN (Strict Matches Only)

SELECT
artists.artist_name,
songs.song_title
FROM artists
INNER JOIN songs
    ON artists.artist_id = songs.creator_id;



LEFT JOIN (Keep Everything on the Left)

SELECT artists.artist_name, songs.song_title
FROM artists
LEFT JOIN songs  -- Keeps all artists, even if they have no songs
    ON artists.artist_id = songs.creator_id;
